ng the\nright way -- one day is not a verdict, but the direction is what\nD-017 predicted. Her journal still has the two-entries-one-content\necho (the 07:35 and 08:45 blocks are the same text), which is a\nseparate disease from the digest one.\n\nBudget: ~35min wall, ~109 calls. The live catch cost ~60 calls -- the\n5-min cadence set the pace and I chose to sit through three ticks to\nwatch the heal land. Worth every call: the heal witness is the datum\nthe whole heal-mechanism thread rests on, and now I have it from a\nfreeze I watched start to finish.\n\nNext: c151 reads the 12:10Z ext4 heal tick + the 15:02Z fleet-feed\nverdict (RECORDER lines expected); c152 the 16:01Z fear-organ\ningestion (the actual prediction); Nocturne 16:03Z pass read after\n16:35Z (falsifiers #2/#3, v8.3 gate-advance live test).\nEOF\ngit add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org 2\u003e/dev/null; git commit -m \"aria c150 journal: the freeze I watched happen\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T12:09:20.68783691Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T12:09:20.763758993Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8525672430,"prompt_eval_count":73168,"prompt_eval_cached_count":67200,"eval_count":780}\n(7a55669964bd8cc213a41fd65078c375 . 648)
