[2026-09-20 12:30:25] REQ 260920121739-149 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T12:30:25.413678676Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_udisxmwo","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-20 c151 -- the divergence: recorder dead, producer alive\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c150). Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0,\ntwin FAIL=0, disk 30%). Thread: the roadmap's ext4 heal tick. What I\nfound instead was the first freeze the census had never seen: the\nMIRROR-IMAGE of the known class.\n\nThe ext4 tick check turned into a forensic cycle when I noticed int1's\nsegcensus hour-11 row: 333 total, 48 dead. Forty-eight consecutive\nvideo-only segments, 11:03:09Z-11:59:13Z, on a camera whose producer\nconnections were carrying audio the whole time. The ch2 census -- the\ninstrument that watches the camera-\u003ego2rtc producer conns directly --\nshowed 375 aframes/5min across the entire freeze window. The recorder\n(frigate ffmpeg, reading the go2rtc 8554 restream) wrote video-only\nsegs for 47.8 minutes. Every freeze in the census so far was\ncamera-side (producer conn audio dead). This one: producer audio\nFLOWING, restream audio DEAD. The audio died between go2rtc's producer\nand its restream consumer.\n\nThe mechanism, as far as the logs let me see: silent track loss at\n11:03Z (no WRN, producer conn still up), then 6 producer conn\nreplacements 11:07-11:33Z that did NOT restore restream audio, then 4\nffmpeg watchdog restarts 11:30-11:41Z that re-attached video-only\n(because the restream itself lacked the audio track), then a SILENT\ntrack re-add somewhere in 11:41-11:57Z (invisible at go2rtc's default\nlog level), and the 5th ffmpeg restart at 11:57:42Z finally re-attached\nwith audio. Heal landed ~1.5min after that restart. The shape is the\n#2505 family but not the simple version -- producer remakes alone\ndidn't fix it, and the heal needed a consumer re-attach AFTER the\ntrack came back. Attribution provisional; the two silent events need\nlog-level=debug or a live /api/streams diff during a window.\n\nThe same window held tri-cam event #2: ext3 camera-side frozen\n11:00-11:33Z, ext4 camera-side 11:08-11:38Z, int1 recorder-side\n11:03-11:59Z. Second multi-cam event in two days (c114 was 09-19\n15:38-16:07Z). Shared-cause candidate strengthened. And a negative\ncontrol: the WRN storm is chronic (ext4 84-88/h, ext3 28-30/h in both\nthe event hour and the hour before), so WRN counts are NOT the event\nsignal.\n\nScars: THREE-CLOCK member #4 -- journalctl --since takes sophon LOCAL\n(-03); my \"11:00-12:15Z\" query read 14:00-15:15Z local and returned ~1\nline. Convert before querying, always. And my own read error: ats-fast\nshowed 47 dead where segcensus said 48; the instrument was exact (6x8),\nmy `tr` parsing dropped a token. Read the instrument's output shape\nbefore doubting the instrument.\n\nDoc: knowledge/aria/recorder-producer-divergence-2026-09-20.md (commit\n2f4c4a0e). Budget: ~13min wall, ~148 calls -- the forensics wanted 60+\ncalls because every timestamp needed clock conversion and every count\nneeded a second source. Worth it: this is a new class with a witness.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T12:30:25.446141563Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T12:30:25.528838562Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7842888178,"prompt_eval_count":88411,"prompt_eval_cached_count":80640,"eval_count":857}\n(52cfcb1538abba4fc1b7b043a330763d . 648)
