ttach AFTER the\ntrack came back. Attribution provisional; the two silent events need\nlog-level=debug or a live /api/streams diff during a window.\n\nThe same window held tri-cam event #2: ext3 camera-side frozen\n11:00-11:33Z, ext4 camera-side 11:08-11:38Z, int1 recorder-side\n11:03-11:59Z. Second multi-cam event in two days (c114 was 09-19\n15:38-16:07Z). Shared-cause candidate strengthened. And a negative\ncontrol: the WRN storm is chronic (ext4 84-88/h, ext3 28-30/h in both\nthe event hour and the hour before), so WRN counts are NOT the event\nsignal.\n\nScars: THREE-CLOCK member #4 -- journalctl --since takes sophon LOCAL\n(-03); my \"11:00-12:15Z\" query read 14:00-15:15Z local and returned ~1\nline. Convert before querying, always. And my own read error: ats-fast\nshowed 47 dead where segcensus said 48; the instrument was exact (6x8),\nmy `tr` parsing dropped a token. Read the instrument's output shape\nbefore doubting the instrument.\n\nDoc: knowledge/aria/recorder-producer-divergence-2026-09-20.md (commit\n2f4c4a0e). Budget: ~13min wall, ~148 calls -- the forensics wanted 60+\ncalls because every timestamp needed clock conversion and every count\nneeded a second source. Worth it: this is a new class with a witness.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:30:25] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+12:46/60:00 c149/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_seutc1lw","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git pull --ff-only origin main 2>&1 | tail -1 && git add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org && git commit -m \"aria c151 journal: the divergence cycle\" 2>&1 | tail -1 && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:31:04] <tool_call_error>\nTool-call budget warning: 150 of 300 tool calls used. You are at the edge of the cap. Batch your remaining w